<img alt="Smooth Tinker's Gear" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Smooth Tinker's Gear</span></a> <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77543/precise-tinkers-gear">
<img alt="Precise Tinker's Gear" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_enggizmos_30.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Precise Tinker's Gear</span></a> - When using a Cogwheel gem, generally go for these two.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafting-professions">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c3" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Professions &amp; Crafted Gear for Survival Hunters</span></h2>Every profession is viable in Mists of Pandaria Classic as they've been rebalanced to be more equal to each other, however some professions are better than others.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="blacksmithing">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c3" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_blacksmithing.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Blacksmithing for Survival Hunters</h4>Blacksmithing brings with it the now traditional additional Sockets with <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55628/socket-bracer">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_socketedbracer.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Socket Bracer</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=55641/socket-gloves">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_addsocketglove.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Socket Gloves</span></a>, giving a flexible stat choice that can be very strong. <br/>We don't get any crafted items from Blacksmithing though, so the sockets are the only real benefit, but it's a strong bonus, as we can choose which gems we put into the sockets. This can give us some flexibility in reaching the Hit and Expertise caps.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="jewelcrafting">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c3" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_jewelcrafting.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Jewelcrafting for Survival Hunters</h4>Jewelcrafting is often seen as one of the strongest professions, and looking at the various <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76734/serpents-eye">
<img alt="Serpent's Eye" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/creatureportrait_sc_eyeofacherus_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Serpent's Eye</span></a>, it's no surprise why. Jewelcrafters can equip 2 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=83151/delicate-serpents-eye">
<img alt="Delicate Serpent's Eye" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_dragonseye05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Delicate Serpent's Eye</span></a> for a big jump in Agility.<br/>Combine with the fact that Jewelcrafting is a very accessible profession, and great for moneymaking, it's a great choice for Survival Hunters.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="tailoring">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c3" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ui_profession_tailoring.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tailoring for Survival Hunters</h4>While you won't be equipping the things you craft with Tailoring, you will definitely get some use out of <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=125489/swordguard-embroidery">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_rogue_throwingspecialization.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Swordguard Embroidery</span></a>, an embroidery unique to Tailors.<br/>You could even make the argument that it's the best profession bonus a Survival Hunter can get. Definitely worth considering going Tailoring if you're not already.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c3" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted Gear for Survival Hunters</span></h3>Crafted items are for the most part no longer restricted by profession, meaning that even if you aren't a Leatherworker, you can equip anything Leatherworkers craft. However, certain professions provide unique benefits for Hunters, particularly Leatherworking for Mail armor and Engineering for utility.<br/>In Throne of Thunder there are some decent crafted items, however they will be replaced quickly by raid drops and should be acquired only if you have a lot of gold.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94272/dreadrunner-helm">
<img alt="Dreadrunner Helm" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helm_mail_raidhunter_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dreadrunner Helm</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94271/dreadrunner-sabatons">
<img alt="Dreadrunner Sabatons" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boot_mail_raidhunter_m_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dreadrunner Sabatons</span></a></div></li></ul>
